"""Withdraw the editor's Download and Upload entries from the explorer menu.

Essilor, 2026-10-30: a right click on a file in the workspace takes it to the
person's own machine. That path is not the network - it rides the session the
browser already has, so the egress profile of a regulated project does not
touch it - and this editor has no option to turn it off. The option exists in
a competing product, and the request upstream (microsoft/vscode#296374, opened
19 February 2026) has no comment, no milestone and no owner.

So it is withdrawn here, at build time, in the one minified file the browser
loads. Two calls register the two menu items, and each is prefixed with a
falsy guard: `0&&f(...)` is valid JavaScript inside the comma chain they live
in, it never calls, and nothing else about the bundle moves. Deleting the
calls instead would mean balancing parentheses inside minified code, which is
how a patch stops being reviewable.

The anchors are the names that come from the source rather than from the
minifier - `appendMenuItem`, `ExplorerContext`, the group `5b_importexport` -
so they survive a version bump that renames every local variable. And the
count is asserted: exactly two matches, or this exits non-zero and no image is
produced. A patch against code we do not own has to fail loudly, because the
alternative is an image that quietly serves the button again.

What this does not do, and it has to be said next to what it does: the person
still has a terminal in that container, so somebody determined keeps what they
can already read. This removes the gesture, which is the volume. And it does
not stop a drag and drop into the explorer - that is a different handler, not
this menu item.
"""

import re
import sys
from pathlib import Path

BUNDLE = Path("/opt/openvscode-server/out/vs/code/browser/workbench/workbench.js")

# <local>.appendMenuItem(<local>.ExplorerContext,{group:"5b_importexport",order:10,
ANCHOR = re.compile(
    r'([A-Za-z_$][\w$]*)\.appendMenuItem\('
    r'([A-Za-z_$][\w$]*)\.ExplorerContext,\{group:"5b_importexport",order:(?:10|20),'
)

source = BUNDLE.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
found = ANCHOR.findall(source)
if len(found) != 2:
    print(
        f"noryx: expected 2 file-transfer menu registrations in {BUNDLE}, found {len(found)}.\n"
        "The editor's bundle changed shape. Read the new registrations before shipping an\n"
        "image: the Download and Upload entries of the explorer context menu must not come\n"
        "back silently.",
        file=sys.stderr,
    )
    raise SystemExit(1)

patched = ANCHOR.sub(lambda m: "0&&" + m.group(0), source)
if patched == source:
    print("noryx: the guard was not inserted", file=sys.stderr)
    raise SystemExit(1)

BUNDLE.write_text(patched, encoding="utf-8")
print("noryx: withdrew the explorer's Download and Upload entries (2 registrations)")
